AB  - Defect diagnosis in electrical equipment is critical for effective grid management. In knowledge-intensive scenarios, large language models (LLMs) often exhibit hallucination issues, limiting their ability to support complex reasoning. This study introduces ElecKG-RAG, a Retrieval-Augmented Generation framework that integrates knowledge graphs to enhance LLM performance. ElecKG-RAG extracts relevant subgraphs from comprehensive knowledge graphs, trans-forming them into high-quality reasoning paths to enable accurate and interpretable diagnostics. The framework employs an ”extraction-scoring-reordering” mechanism, utilizing a multidimensional scoring and reverse ranking fusion (RRF) algorithm to identify optimal reasoning paths. Experiments on a power defect question-answering dataset, using LLaMA3-70B, demonstrate that ElecKG-RAG achieves an accuracy of 86.1%, significantly surpassing traditional RAG and other baseline models, particularly in multi-hop reasoning tasks requiring complex logic. This research offers a robust technical solution for the safe and reliable application of LLMs in critical infrastructure, such as power systems.
