AB  - As enterprise digital transformation continues to advance, the demand for efficient and reliable knowledge services is increasing. Conventional enterprise support methods often suffer from scattered knowledge resources, inefficient manual search, and limited knowledge reuse. To address these issues, this paper presents an enterprise question-answering approach that combines large language models (LLMs) with retrieval-augmented generation (RAG). The proposed approach covers document parsing, knowledge base construction, text embedding, semantic retrieval, reranking, and grounded answer generation. Experimental results and application practice show that the system improves answer accuracy, response efficiency, and knowledge utilization in enterprise scenarios. The study offers a practical reference for developing domain-oriented intelligent Q&A services in organizational environments.
