AB  - The exponential growth of unstructured data presents a serious challenge in the retrieval of precise and relevant information, with traditional keyword-based search methods faced with challenges in searching paraphrased or long queries. At the same time, generative AI models are prone to generating inaccurate results because they rely on fixed training data. For this problem, the system proposed here presents a retrieval augmented generation (RAG)-based chatbot system that incorporates eye power generation principles, thus enhancing contextual understanding through semantic searching. ChromaDB, a vector database with dense embeddings generated by transformer models, is the core of the system. Queries entered by the user are semantically searched against the data in storage, and responses are generated with the assistance of a Large Language Model (LLM) accessed through the Gemini API or a local transformer-based model. The system is coded in Python with FastAPI, which supports modular and scalable deployment. The innovation is the use of retrieval-augmented generation with multimodal capabilities, which supports precise, domain-dependent, and personal interactions in a wide range of applications such as customer support, education, and multimodal AI tasks.
