AB  - The abundance of false information on the internet makes it difficult to find trustworthy medical information, particularly in specialized fields like physiotherapy. Despite their strength, Large Language Models (LLMs) are not suitable for giving medical advice due to their propensity to hallucinate. We introduce PhysioRAG, a RetrievalAugmented Generation (RAG) system that provides verifiable and evidence-based physiotherapy information. Our contribution is an end-to-end methodology for building a domain-specific chatbot, including the curation of a knowledge base from over 20,000 PubMed Central articles. The system incorporates a Query Transformation step, where an LLM reformulates user questions into technical biomedical search phrases to improve retrieval accuracy. PhysioRAG links all generated statements to their corresponding PubMed sources, further enforcing citation-grounded responses. This work details the system architecture and evaluation, demonstrating a robust and transparent solution for trustworthy medical information delivery.
