AB  - This paper presents JuristRAG, a retrieval augmented generation (RAG) system that is designed to answer queries related to Bangladeshi criminal statutes. Existing chatbots are prone to hallucination and provide factually incorrect answers when applied to sensitive legal domains. To address this issue, we propose an advanced retrieval pipeline which uses a combination of iterative retrieval and an LLM-guided query decomposition, supported by a section-wise preprocessing of the laws. Our dataset uses three fundamental Bangladeshi laws: the Code of Criminal Procedure, the Penal Code and the Special Powers Act. We evaluated JuristRAG using automated metrics (faithfulness, cosine similarity, BERTScore and ROGUE) and human assessment. The results demonstrate that our proposed pipeline consistently outperforms traditional RAG pipelines, yielding better results, higher contextual accuracy, semantic alignment and clarity in responses. This work contributes towards increasing legal information accessibility and establishes a foundation for AI-driven legal assistance in Bangladesh.
